      "From 27 January to 13 February 1979 the Third General Conference of the Latin American Episcopate meets in Puebla on the theme of evangelization in the present and future of Latin America. Pope John Paul II, on his first trip abroad, inaugurates it after a Mass at the Basilica of Guadalupe; of 356 participants, 221 are bishops. The final document renews Medellín's concern for the poor and names a 'preferential option for the poor', alongside tensions between those wishing to deepen Medellín and those seeking to correct its excesses.",
