      "Born in 1626 in Vilaflor, Tenerife, Pedro de San José de Betancur left the Canary Islands at 23 for New Spain and settled in Santiago de los Caballeros (today Antigua Guatemala), where he died on 25 April 1667. A Franciscan tertiary, he founded the first hospital for convalescents there and a school for adults and children open to all, regardless of race or sex, and the Bethlehemite Order grew from his work. Known as Hermano Pedro, he is considered the first saint of Guatemala and Central America (canonized in 2002).",
