      "Stanley Rother, a priest from Oklahoma, had served as a missionary in the Tz'utujil Maya parish of Santiago Atitlán during the Guatemalan civil war. On 28 July 1981 he was murdered in his rectory. He had written of the dangers facing his people and the church. Pope Francis confirmed in December 2016 that he died a martyr, and he was beatified in Oklahoma City on 23 September 2017, the first U.S.-born priest and martyr beatified by the Catholic Church. The case is a symbol of the violence suffered by church workers in Guatemala.",
