      "In 1958 a small group of Mennonites from Chihuahua state in Mexico crosses into what was then British Honduras to found a farming community at Spanish Lookout, on land that was dense rainforest. They were followed by about 1,700 more from the Mexican colonies. Spanish Lookout was settled by the Kleine Gemeinde, while Old Colony Mennonites founded Blue Creek and Shipyard in the same year. The settlements, speaking Plautdietsch, range from modern to very traditional and are central to Belizean agriculture.",
