      "The poet and priest Ernesto Cardenal founds a contemplative and artistic community on the Solentiname islands of Lake Nicaragua in 1965, living there until 1977. Cardenal became a leading voice of liberation theology, joined the Sandinistas, and served as Nicaragua's minister of culture from 1979 to 1987. Pope John Paul II banned him from administering the sacraments in 1984, and Pope Francis rehabilitated him in 2019. Solentiname became a symbol of the meeting of faith, art and revolution in Central America.",
