      "The Scottish colony of Caledonia, founded in 1698 at New Edinburgh on the Gulf of Darién, was meant to be a Presbyterian settlement as well as a trading venture. One minister of the first expedition died at sea; in July 1699 the General Assembly's commission sent four more, Alexander Shields, Francis Borland, Alexander Dalgleish and Archibald Stobo, who formed the Presbytery of Caledonia. The Covenanter Shields, sometimes called the Church of Scotland's first foreign missionary, died in 1700. The colony itself failed.",
